    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0521" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330/8–1753: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Mission at the
                        United Nations</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-08-17T18:52:00-04:00">August 17,
                            1953—6:52 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>66. Re SC election. Since Turk decision to run dependent on indication of success
                    based on preliminary soundings (Ankara’s 189) suggest you approach other
                    delegations on matter working closely with Turkish delegation. Believe UK and
                    France should be approached soonest.</p>
                <p>While we will of course give Turkey firm support we continue hope it will make
                    real effort develop own candidacy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
